ty_fundamentals (bounds regular, market_date 2026-11-18), read 05:41 CT Thu 19 Nov.", "indices": "CappNotes Closing Look 18 Nov: S&P 500 7,323.63 (-16.90, fifth straight loss), Nasdaq Composite 24,429.89 (+101.50), Dow 50,198.17 (-561.25). Previous closes = close minus the printed point change. StockTitan (CNBC, 5:13 p.m. ET) and TradingKey print the same closes (Nasdaq 24,429.88). SPY 730.20, QQQ 659.51, DIA 501.73 official closes on Robinhood.", "chevron": "18 Nov was Chevron's ex-dividend date ($1.78 a share, Robinhood fundamentals), so about 0.8 points of its 4.7% drop is the dividend coming out of the price. The Reel shows the official close-to-close move.", "moves_vs_reports": "Computed moves match the reports: NVDA -2.89, AMD +5.31, UNH -10.21, TGT +4.01, TJX +8.05, PANW +9.90 (CappNotes, StockTitan, TradingKey); TTWO +6.22 (Fox Business: more than 6%, closing at $216.61); NEM -6.05 (Investopedia: more than 6%); BRBR +24.07 (StockTitan). CVX -4.74: StockTitan printed -4.33% at 1:01 p.m. ET; no source printed its close move."}, "story_sources": {"NVDA": "StockTitan 18 Nov live blog (sales more than doubled to $115.8 billion; expects about $130.0 billion next quarter; forecast assumes no data center chip sales in China; Colette Kress interim CEO since Huang resigned 12 Nov; +2.79% premarket, -2.89% at close). TradingKey 18 Nov (revenue +103% to $115.8 billion, adjusted EPS $2.68, both topped expectations; chair Harvey Jones said on the call the board has no intention of reinstating Huang and has hired a search firm). CappNotes (erased premarket gains despite Tuesday's beat). Investopedia via Yahoo (ended down nearly 3%). Robinhood earnings calendar: EPS 2.68 vs 2.47 estimate.", "AMD": "CappNotes (AMD +5.31%: Nvidia outlook eased demand worries; completed its $2.9 billion Taalas acquisition; AVGO +3.64%). TradingKey (AMD +5.31%, Broadcom +3.65%, no reason given; Philadelphia Semiconductor Index +0.1%, 15 of 30 members up). Investopedia (AMD up 5%, Broadcom up 4%; Marvell down 2%, Intel and Micron down 1%). The headline states only the two moves because chip stocks were mixed.", "UNH": "StockTitan (CMS proposed rule announced Monday to recover more improper payments to Medicare Advantage plans using audit error extrapolation from 2018 payments; estimated $90.2 billion recovered from 2027 through 2036; comments due 19 Jan 2027; UNH -10.21%, HUM -12.98%, second straight daily fall). CappNotes (CMS proposed CRUSH rule, Medicare Advantage audits; UNH biggest Dow drag; ELV -7.63%, CNC -7.03%). Investopedia (UNH down 10%, biggest Dow decliner; Humana down 13%, leading S&P 500 decliners).", "TTWO": "Fox Business 18 Nov 9:04 p.m. ET (shares surged more than 6% on Wednesday, closing at $216.61; rolling midnight launch ahead of its Thursday, Nov. 19 U.S. release, per Reuters; 13-year wait; Metacritic 99 per Reuters; Sensor Tower: roughly 17 million copies sold, more than $1.65 billion, as of Wednesday). StockTitan (Take-Two +8.37% at 11:05 a.m.; GTA VI scheduled to launch Thursday).", "TGT": "StockTitan (Q3 net sales $27.1 billion, up 7.1%; comparable sales up 5.6%; EPS $2.65 including $0.50 from tariff refunds; raised full-year sales outlook; +4.01% at close). CappNotes (best sales growth in five years; raised full-year EPS outlook to $10.65 to $11.40). Robinhood: 52-week high 171.91 set on 18 Nov.", "TJX": "CappNotes (TJX +8.05%; revenue $15.95 billion vs $15.82 billion estimate; full-year EPS outlook raised to $5.17 to $5.20). StockTitan (Q3 comparable sales up 4%, above plan; EPS $1.39, or $1.34 without tariff refunds). Investopedia (results topped Wall Street expectations).", "PANW": "CappNotes (PANW +9.90% in the regular session; cybersecurity rally tied to CISA urging organizations to immediately patch the Java4Shell vulnerability; S +10.35%, CRWD +7.95%; after the bell: fiscal Q1 adjusted EPS $1.05 vs 97-cent estimate, raised guidance, $4.5 billion all-stock deal for Applied Compute). Investopedia (PANW soared 10%, CRWD 8%, FTNT 6% amid mounting fears about cyber threats). StockTitan (fiscal Q1 revenue up 39% to $3.44 billion; raised fiscal 2027 revenue forecast; +9.08% after hours at 7:59 p.m.). Search results seen: CISA alert of 17 Nov 'Critical Java Vulnerability Requires Immediate Patching'; SecurityWeek and Techzine on Java4Shell; Quantisnow 'Cybersecurity stocks rallied hours before Palo Alto's report'.", "CVX": "CappNotes (WTI -3.20% settled at $83.26, its lowest close since Aug. 26, after a 3.38 million-barrel US crude build; energy sector -3.27%, the worst). Investopedia (WTI fell 3.7% to $82.85; down about 20% since the start of the month; energy the worst S&P 500 sector). StockTitan/CNBC (WTI fell more than 4% to $82.19 at 12:54 p.m.; Chevron -4.33% and ExxonMobil -3.56% at 1:01 p.m.; Chevron weighed on the Dow).", "NEM": "Investopedia (gold fell 3.5% to $3,730 an ounce, lowest in 14 months; Newmont and Freeport-McMoRan each down more than 6%). CappNotes (gold futures -3.50% settled at $3,728.80, lowest since September 2025; silver -4.84%, copper -5.24%).", "BRBR": "BellRing Brands release of 18 Nov (SEC 8-K exhibit 99.1): Q4 net sales $692.0 million, up 7% (6.8%); Premier Protein net sales +7.1%; net earnings $35.6 million vs $59.6 million; adjusted EBITDA $66.4 million vs $117.4 million; fiscal 2027 outlook net sales $2.32-$2.42 billion, adjusted EBITDA $310-$350 million; withdrew long-term targets. StockTitan (+24.07% at close; same sales figures). Robinhood: market cap about $1.6 billion, 52-week high 33.56, low 7.33."}}